    Adapter design pattern is one of the structural design pattern
    It act as a bridge between two incompatible interfaces to make them work together without
    changing their source code.

    Adapter Design Pattern is used to convert incompatible interfaces into a compatible one without changing their source code.
    It is one of the most commonly used Structural Design Patterns in Spring Framework and Microservices Architecture.



    Definition : Adapter design pattern allows two different classes with incompatible interfaces to
    communicate with each other without modifying their code.

    when to use Adapter design pattern ?
    1.> when you want to integrate old code with new code
    2.> when two classes have incompatible interfaces
    3.> when you want reuse existing code

    Advantages ?
    1.> Loose coupling
    2.> code reusability
    3.> improve flexibility
    4.> Easy integration of legacy code

    In spring boot Adapter design patterns used :
    1.> Handler Adapter
    2.> View Resolver Adapter
    3.> wenMVCConfigureAdapter

    What is HandlerAdapter?
👉 HandlerAdapter acts as a bridge between DispatcherServlet and Controller Methods
It converts HTTP Requests into Controller Method Calls automatically.

How it Works Internally?
Step-by-Step Flow:

DispatcherServlet receives HTTP Request
It identifies the correct Controller
But Controller methods are not directly callable because they are just normal Java methods
So, HandlerAdapter converts HTTP request into a format that Controller understands
Then it calls the respective Controller method

What is ViewResolverAdapter?
👉 It converts the View Name returned from the Controller into an actual View Object.
How Adapter Works Here?
Controller returns "home" as String
DispatcherServlet doesn't know what "home" means
ViewResolverAdapter converts "home" into home.jsp or home.html automatically

